& [ConceptualModel] defines distinct data subjects
  + [digest_plan] is strict caller syntax selecting one transform profile, one nonzero correlation identity, and one exact encoding profile
  + [inventory_assembly] is the complete owned supplied input and lineage root
  + [inventory_member] is one ordered complete root, directory, or regular-file carrier
  + [topology_observation] is the semantic record exposed by one inventory member
  + [stream_fact] is one ordered stream record nested in an observation
  + [canonical_update_stream] is the transient exact byte sequence fed incrementally to SHA-256
  + [ordered_inventory_digest] is the 32-byte SHA-256 value represented publicly as lowercase 64-hex
  + [digest_result] is the private output wrapper retaining digest plan, exact profiles, complete assembly, and ordered inventory digest
  + [digest_fault] is one bounded denial record with optional nested topology-form fault only at the current validation boundary
  + [proof_artifact] is test, static boundary record, evidence manifest, audit, solution, or provenance closure outside the runtime result

& [IdentityModel] preserves roles
  + [plan_identity] is commitment_identity and is caller correlation only
  + [transform_identity] is exact result profile cantor-windows-supplied-ordered-topology-inventory-digest/0.1
  + [encoding_identity] is exact encoding profile cantor-ordered-topology-observation-encoding/0.1
  + [sequence_identity] is exact assembly member count plus ordered observation values under encoding_identity
  + [member_identity] remains the nested carrier identity and is retained but not encoded as proof lineage
  + [file_identity] is volume_serial plus decoded 16-byte file_id and is committed observation content
  + [content_identity] is optional decoded 32-byte content_sha256 and is committed observation content
  + [digest_identity] is encoding_identity plus ordered_inventory_digest under ordinary SHA-256 collision assumptions
  - never: substitute one identity role for another because two roles share an integer, string, or digest representation

& [OwnershipAndCardinality] are exact
  + one digest_plan governs one successful digest_result
  + one digest_result owns exactly one complete inventory_assembly
  + one inventory_assembly owns one or more ordered inventory_members because the root is mandatory
  + each inventory_member exposes exactly one topology_observation
  + each topology_observation owns zero or more ordered stream_facts
  + one successful transform derives exactly one ordered_inventory_digest
  + failure returns exactly one digest_fault and no digest_result
  + proof_artifacts cite runtime subjects but are not embedded in the digest subject

& [RelationModel] distinguishes containment, derivation, and exclusion
  + digest_result contains digest_plan, inventory_assembly, encoding_identity, transform_identity, and ordered_inventory_digest
  + inventory_assembly contains ordered inventory_members
  + inventory_member exposes topology_observation without transferring or reconstructing lineage
  + topology_observation contains ordered stream_facts
  + canonical_update_stream derives from encoding_identity, sequence cardinality, ordered topology_observations, and their stream_facts
  + ordered_inventory_digest derives from canonical_update_stream
  + digest_plan correlates digest_result but does not contribute commitment_identity to canonical_update_stream
  + inventory_assembly preserves proof lineage but does not contribute carrier-only lineage to canonical_update_stream

& [LogicalCanonicalRecord] is one exact sequence
  + [domain_record] is exact encoding-profile ASCII bytes followed by zero
  + [count_record] is one u64 big-endian entry count
  + [entry_record] begins with entry-start and encodes every declared observation field in the closed field order
  + [stream_sequence_record] encodes one u64 count and each stream record in existing order
  + [option_record] is absent byte zero or present byte one followed by the value
  + [text_record] is u64 big-endian UTF-8 byte count plus exact UTF-8 bytes
  + [identity_record] is exact decoded 16 bytes
  + [digest_record] is exact decoded 32 bytes
  + [integer_record] is fixed u32 or u64 big endian
  + [enum_record] is one declared nonzero byte
  + each field occurs exactly once and no implicit padding, delimiter, discriminant, default, normalization, or serializer metadata exists

& [TransformModel] separates query, validation, encoding, and result formation
  + [decode_plan] is bytes to validated digest_plan or digest_fault and has no external effect
  + [validate_assembly] is immutable inventory_assembly inspection to validated correlations or digest_fault
  + [encode_observation] is topology_observation plus private hash sink to ordered canonical updates or digest_fault
  + [encode_stream_fact] is stream_fact plus private hash sink to ordered canonical updates or digest_fault
  + [finalize_digest] is private hash sink to ordered_inventory_digest
  + [form_result] is validated digest_plan plus consumed inventory_assembly plus ordered_inventory_digest to digest_result
  + [public_transform] composes the preceding pure operations in fail-closed order and exposes Result digest_result or digest_fault
  + every helper remains subject local and private unless the canonical specification explicitly states otherwise

& [StateAndLifecycle] are bounded
  + [unparsed] plan bytes exist outside transform authority
  + [plan_validated] exact profiles and nonzero identity are accepted
  + [assembly_validated] profile, count, root, ordinal, current forms, and accounting are accepted
  + [hashing] canonical_update_stream is being supplied to a private accumulator and no public intermediate exists
  + [succeeded] one complete digest_result owns the input and digest
  + [failed] one digest_fault exists and the caller receives no digest result or partial byte state
  + [superseded_profile] is never inferred; it requires new source and authority
  + no persisted runtime lifecycle, mutation lifecycle, receipt lifecycle, or cleanup lifecycle exists in this slice

& [PhysicalModel] is in-memory Rust only
  + digest_plan is a strict serde-deserialized private-field struct with immutable getters
  + inventory_assembly is the existing output-only Rust type consumed by value after validation
  + digest_result is a private-field Serialize-only Rust struct and does not derive Deserialize or Default
  + canonical_update_stream is never stored as one collection; private writer methods call sha2 update with stack arrays and borrowed UTF-8 slices
  + decoded identity and digest values use fixed 16-byte and 32-byte stack arrays
  + tag values are private named constants grouped by grammar namespace
  + digest_fault is a bounded serializable value with a closed code and optional nested topology fault
  + no database row, file, cache, index, network message, FFI structure, Windows handle, or public canonical byte buffer is introduced

& [ProvenanceModel] is explicit
  + source snapshot and SJS artifact hashes govern implementation authority
  + digest_result provenance is the complete retained inventory_assembly and exact plan
  + digest bytes attest only to encoded observation content and order under encoding_identity
  + proof_artifacts attest implementation behavior and remain separate from runtime lineage
  + stale source, prerequisite authority, canonical specification, implementation, or proof invalidates readiness according to its governing record
  - never: infer physical provenance from retained supplied lineage or cryptographic determinism

& [IntegrityRules] close illegal states
  + exact profiles and nonzero commitment identity
  + exact assembly profile and representable equal count
  + root first with exact root shape and one-based ordinal correspondence
  + current topology validation for every observation
  + checked regular-file byte recomputation equal to assembly total
  + exact closed grammar and all semantic fields present once
  + fixed-width lowercase hex validation before decoding
  + complete assembly retained on success and no partial result on failure
  + zero effects, unsafe, dependency delta, platform calls, and whole-inventory buffer

& [AccessPatterns] are minimal and sufficient
  + public create operation is one pure transform from plan bytes and complete assembly to result or fault
  + public read access is immutable getters over result profile, encoding profile, plan, assembly, and digest
  + no public update, delete, decode, rehydrate, alternate constructor, normalization, negotiation, or comparison operation exists
  + proof access uses tests and evidence artifacts rather than runtime mutation or introspection hooks

& [DataDesignQualityGate] passes
  + [identity_check] is passed with correlation, file, content, sequence, profile, and digest roles distinct
  + [relationship_check] is passed with containment, exposure, derivation, correlation, and exclusion explicit
  + [cardinality_check] is passed with one result, one assembly, ordered nonempty members, ordered streams, and atomic fault alternative
  + [transform_check] is passed with validation, encoding, hashing, and formation responsibilities separated
  + [state_check] is passed with no public partial-success state
  + [lifecycle_check] is passed with profile evolution and downstream receipt work outside authority
  + [provenance_check] is passed with retained lineage distinct from digest subject and proof lineage
  + [physical_check] is passed with bounded in-memory Rust representation and no persistence or effects
  + [requirement_coverage] is M2B-SOTID-001 through M2B-SOTID-015
  + [source_revision_required] is false
  + [next] canonical specification, justification, plan, registry, matrix, slice, phase lock, and signature
  + [implementation_authority] is absent
